-- A binding of a field accessor over a neural read whose accessor implies a
-- constructor (task scene-rebuild-with-float-leaf-loses-probability): `px`
-- is only defined on Obj, so binding `p = px (readObj s)` constrains every
-- world to the Obj flag, exactly as `px o` read inside a body does. The
-- answer is the sub-probability of the Obj arm (generate raises on Nil,
-- hence no-normalization).
-- Object plan [Nil, Obj | Red, Green | mu, sigma] = [0.3, 0.7, 0.4, 0.6, 0.0, 1.0].
-- p(-0.5) = 0.7 phi(0.5)   (dim 1)
data Color = Red | Green
data Object = Nil | Obj color::Color, px::Float
neural readObj :: (Symbol -> Object)
main s = draw p = px (readObj s) in p - 1.0
